1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,944
Meet FloorCheck: the AI floor-plan
auditor for equipment lenders.

2
00:00:04,844 --> 00:00:07,818
When a dealer sells a
tractor the lender paid for,

3
00:00:07,818 --> 00:00:10,554
and keeps the money,
that's called sold out of

4
00:00:10,554 --> 00:00:10,910
trust.

5
00:00:10,910 --> 00:00:12,873
It's the classic floor-plan loss.

6
00:00:12,873 --> 00:00:15,312
And lenders usually find out weeks later,

7
00:00:15,312 --> 00:00:17,572
from an auditor walking the lot with a

8
00:00:17,572 --> 00:00:18,166
clipboard.

9
00:00:18,566 --> 00:00:22,501
Here's a lender's floor-plan
book: forty-two financed units

10
00:00:22,501 --> 00:00:25,968
across three dealers, four
point six million dollars

11
00:00:25,968 --> 00:00:26,768
outstanding.

12
00:00:27,068 --> 00:00:32,396
One click hands the audit to an always-on
agent with its own computer on Agent37.

13
00:00:32,396 --> 00:00:36,540
It opens each dealer's inventory
page in its own browser, reads

14
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:40,223
every listing, and writes what
it found to a file on its

15
00:00:40,223 --> 00:00:40,749
machine.

16
00:00:40,749 --> 00:00:45,354
This is a recording of a real run:
forty-six seconds, nine tool calls.

17
00:00:45,553 --> 00:00:49,864
FloorCheck pulls that file back and
matches every financed serial number.

18
00:00:49,864 --> 00:00:52,344
Thirty-five units are verified on the lot.

19
00:00:52,344 --> 00:00:55,592
But three are listed as sold
while the advance is still

20
00:00:55,592 --> 00:00:59,077
unpaid: two hundred sixty-two
thousand dollars, sold out of

21
00:00:59,077 --> 00:00:59,431
trust.

22
00:00:59,431 --> 00:01:02,089
Plus three units that
aren't listed anywhere.

23
00:01:02,389 --> 00:01:06,563
Every exception is defensible:
the listing exactly as the dealer

24
00:01:06,563 --> 00:01:11,128
published it, the URL, a timestamp,
and a field-by-field match against

25
00:01:11,128 --> 00:01:11,845
the ledger.

26
00:01:12,146 --> 00:01:15,814
And Monid pulls live market comps
for that exact model, so the

27
00:01:15,814 --> 00:01:19,364
lender knows what it would
actually recover: about forty-two

28
00:01:19,364 --> 00:01:22,618
thousand dollars, against a
seventy-one thousand dollar

29
00:01:22,618 --> 00:01:23,091
advance.

30
00:01:23,491 --> 00:01:26,980
For everything still on the lot,
FloorCheck estimates what the

31
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:30,582
collateral is worth today, so the
lender sees coverage, not just

32
00:01:30,582 --> 00:01:31,145
existence.

33
00:01:31,445 --> 00:01:35,389
It drafts a payoff demand to each dealer,
and the memo for the credit committee.

34
00:01:37,601 --> 00:01:41,859
And it schedules itself on Agent37,
to run every night at 2 AM.

35
00:01:43,258 --> 00:01:48,512
Under the hood: Agent37 runs the agent,
its computer, and its nightly schedule.

36
00:01:48,512 --> 00:01:51,571
Monid finds and runs the
market-data scrapers.

37
00:01:51,571 --> 00:01:55,562
And InstaCloud hosts the app,
with its Postgres audit trail.

38
00:01:55,862 --> 00:01:58,771
FloorCheck walks every
lot, every night, in under

39
00:01:58,771 --> 00:02:01,502
a minute, instead of an
auditor driving lot to

40
00:02:01,502 --> 00:02:01,740
lot.
